1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,526
Citibank meant to wire 7.8 million

2
00:00:02,526 --> 00:00:04,830
dollars in interest for Revlon.

3
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:05,424
Instead,

4
00:00:05,424 --> 00:00:08,397
it accidentally wired almost 900 million

5
00:00:08,397 --> 00:00:09,660
of its own money.

6
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:12,478
Here is Exhibit Figure 1 from court.

7
00:00:12,478 --> 00:00:15,139
Three reviewers checked PRINCIPAL,

8
00:00:15,139 --> 00:00:17,487
but missed that FRONT and FUND

9
00:00:17,487 --> 00:00:19,444
also had to be checked to

10
00:00:19,444 --> 00:00:20,540
stop the wire.

11
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:23,057
Ten firms refused to return over

12
00:00:23,057 --> 00:00:24,630
500 million dollars.

13
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:26,754
A trial judge let them keep

14
00:00:26,754 --> 00:00:28,956
it in 2021 before an appeals

15
00:00:28,956 --> 00:00:31,630
court reversed the ruling in 2022.

16
00:00:31,630 --> 00:00:33,201
Wall Street never forgot.

17
00:00:33,201 --> 00:00:34,332
By September 2026,

18
00:00:34,332 --> 00:00:37,160
erroneous payment clawback clauses sit inside

19
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:39,800
88 percent of corporate credit agreements.

20
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:42,062
Three human reviewers still missed a

21
00:00:42,062 --> 00:00:43,381
bad software default.

22
00:00:43,381 --> 00:00:45,957
High-stakes systems need clearer screens,

23
00:00:45,957 --> 00:00:47,590
not just extra signatures.
